-- title:
--   Many independent weight-2m modular functions over ℚ̄
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $m\ge 1$ be a natural number. Write $K=\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (the `AlgebraicClosure` of $\mathbb{Q}$), let $j=$ `jqModC` $K$ be the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the image over $K$ of the integral power series `jNum`, and let $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC` $K\,N$ be the intermediate field of $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by the series $j(q^{d})$ for the divisors $d$ of $N$. The assertion is that there exist a natural number $d$ and a family $G\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,d\to F$ such that: (i) $G$ is linearly independent over $K$; (ii) each $G_i$, regarded as a Laurent series, satisfies `IsModPFormFn`, that is $G_i^{6}\,j^{4m}(j-1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $j$ and $G_i^{2}\,j^{m}(j-1728)^{m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$; and (iii) $$(2m-1)\bigl(g(N)-1\bigr)+\lfloor m/2\rfloor\,\nu_2(N)+\lfloor 2m/3\rfloor\,\nu_3(N)+m\,\nu_\infty(N)\le d,$$ where $\nu_2(N)=\#\{x\in\mathbb{Z}/N: x^2+1=0\}$, $\nu_3(N)=\#\{x\in\mathbb{Z}/N: x^2+x+1=0\}$, $\nu_\infty(N)=\sum_{d\mid N}\varphi(\gcd(d,N/d))$ is `cuspCount`, and $g(N)=1+\psi(N)/12-\nu_2(N)/4-\nu_3(N)/3-\nu_\infty(N)/2$ is `genusFormula` with $\psi(N)=\sum_{d\mid N,\ d\ \text{squarefree}}N/d$; the floors are the natural-number quotients $m/2$ and $2m/3$.
--
--   This is the algebraic-function-field form of the classical lower bound $\dim_{\mathbb{C}} M_{2m}(\Gamma_0(N))\ge (2m-1)(g-1)+\lfloor m/2\rfloor\nu_2+\lfloor 2m/3\rfloor\nu_3+m\nu_\infty$, with holomorphy of weight $2m$ expressed by the integrality conditions of `IsModPFormFn` rather than analytically. It is the statement over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ from which the corresponding assertion over $\mathbb{Q}$, [`ModularCurve.exists_linearIndependent_isModPFormFn_rat_dimFormula_le_card`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_linearIndependent_isModPFormFn_rat_dimFormula_le_card), is obtained.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_linearIndependent_isModPFormFn_algebraicClosure_dimFormula_le_card.lean

